.TH STOP-MU2EDAQ-HEARTBEATMONITOR.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-heartbeatmonitor t01.00.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
stop\-mu2edaq\-heartbeatmonitor.sh \- stop the heartbeat monitor daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B stop\-mu2edaq\-heartbeatmonitor.sh
.RI [ pid_file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Control\-room stop script, run as
.BR "crs\-app stop heartbeatmonitor" .
Reads the PID from
.IR pid_file ,
sends SIGTERM, waits up to
.B CRS_STOP_TIMEOUT
seconds for the process to exit, sends SIGKILL if it has not, and removes the
PID file.
A missing PID file, or one naming a process that no longer exists, is reported
and treated as success.
.PP
The script trusts the PID file: it does not check that the PID belongs to
.BR heartbeat_monitor.py .
The daemon creates that file with mode 0666.
If the file is missing while the monitor is still running (see
.BR start\-mu2edaq\-heartbeatmonitor.sh (1)),
this script reports "not running"; find the process with
.B "pgrep \-af heartbeat_monitor.py"
and kill it by hand.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I pid_file
Default:
.I heartbeat_monitor.pid
in the script's directory.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CRS_STOP_TIMEOUT
Seconds to wait after SIGTERM before SIGKILL.
Default 10.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Stopped, or not running.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS 4
.nf
\&./stop\-mu2edaq\-heartbeatmonitor.sh
CRS_STOP_TIMEOUT=30 ./stop\-mu2edaq\-heartbeatmonitor.sh
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR start\-mu2edaq\-heartbeatmonitor.sh (1),
.BR heartbeat_monitor.py (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ Group, Fermi National Accelerator Laboratory.
